# Control-plane ownership (claudeconf constitution §4.7.1).
#
# These paths are the ones that can WEAKEN the harness: change a gate, silence a scanner,
# widen an exclude, or repoint a pinned tool. Everything here requires review by someone
# other than the change author.
#
# CONFIGURED, NOT ENFORCED. This file alone changes nothing. GitHub only requires these
# reviews once a branch ruleset on `master` is set to: require review from code owners,
# dismiss stale approvals on new pushes, require approval of the most recent push, and
# allow no bypass actors. Until those four are set, this file is documentation.
#
# The default owner is the repository owner because this project currently has one
# maintainer. A single-maintainer CODEOWNERS cannot deliver "review by someone else" --
# that limit is real and is not fixed by this file.

*                                   @nikolaypaskov

# ── CI and the workflow audit configuration ───────────────────────────────────────
/.github/workflows/                 @nikolaypaskov
/.github/dependabot.yml             @nikolaypaskov
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @nikolaypaskov

# ── The harness itself ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/lefthook.yml                       @nikolaypaskov
/.claudeconf/                       @nikolaypaskov

# ── Pinned tool configs: changing these changes what the gates actually check ──────
/rust-toolchain.toml                @nikolaypaskov
/.rustfmt.toml                      @nikolaypaskov
/.clippy.toml                       @nikolaypaskov
/deny.toml                          @nikolaypaskov
/Cargo.lock                         @nikolaypaskov

# ── Heddle's own privacy gates and their recorded baselines ───────────────────────
# A baseline edit can make a removed commercial surface look like it was never there.
/script/heddle/                     @nikolaypaskov

# ── The agent's own permission surface ────────────────────────────────────────────
/.claude/settings.json              @nikolaypaskov
